  "generated_answer": "## Fractions in Class 4 (Primary 4) \u2014 Mathematics\n\nBased on the retrieved curriculum evidence, pupils in Class 4 learn about fractions across three units: **C4-U04 (Fraction)**, **C4-U05 (Operation on Fractions)**, and **C4-U06 (Operation on Fraction \u2013 Multiplication)**.\n\n### Unit C4-U04: Number and Numeration \u2013 FRACTION\n- **C4U04-LO01** \u2014 Simplify like fraction with common denominators.\n- **C4U04-LO02** \u2014 Compare and order like fraction.\n- **C4U04-LO03** \u2014 Identify Equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U04-LO04** \u2014 Relate fractions with denominators up to compare equivalent fraction greater than *(source text appears truncated/incomplete)*.\n\n### Unit C4-U05: Number and Numeration \u2013 OPERATION ON FRACTIONS\n- **C4U05-LO01** \u2014 Add Equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U05-LO02** \u2014 Subtract Equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U05-LO03** \u2014 Solve both Addition and Subtraction of Equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U05-LO04** \u2014 Solve word problems involving Addition and Subtraction of Equivalent fractions.\n\n### Unit C4-U06: Number and Numeration \u2013 Operation on Fraction (Multiplication)\n- **C4U06-LO01** \u2014 Multiply equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U06-LO02** \u2014 Multiply like fractions with denominators up to multiply like fractions with denominators up to multiply related fractions with denominators up to multiply related fractions with denominators up to *(source text is garbled/repetitive and incomplete)*.\n\n### Summary of fraction learning in Class 4\n- **Identify, simplify, compare, and order** like fractions.\n- **Identify equivalent fractions** and relate them (with denominators up to a value not fully specified in the evidence).\n- **Add, subtract, and solve word problems** involving equivalent fractions.\n- **Multiply** equivalent fractions and like/related fractions (with denominators up to a value not fully specified in the evidence).",
